openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:3:Expose explicit ball-valve execution evidence in stable retrieval text so tender vocabulary can retrieve compatible catalog variants without discarding raw catalog evidence.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:7:### Requirement: Preserve raw catalog evidence while adding execution descriptors
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:9:For each catalog ball valve, the system SHALL retain all current raw catalog fields in both dense search text and lexical search text. It SHALL append zero or more stable Russian execution descriptors derived only from explicit product-name or supported-property evidence. The descriptors SHALL not replace, delete, or contradict raw catalog terms.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:11:#### Scenario: Explicit specialised execution
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:13:- **WHEN** a ball-valve catalog record explicitly identifies an underground, regulating, cryogenic, gas-specific, or electric-ready execution
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:16:#### Scenario: No execution evidence
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:18:- **WHEN** a catalog record has no recognised explicit execution evidence
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:19:- **THEN** the system does not invent a specialised execution descriptor
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:23:The system SHALL add `стандартное исполнение` only for a ball valve that has no recognised explicit specialised-execution evidence. When a supported catalog field explicitly states a non-full/reduced passage, the retrieval documents SHALL also expose the synonymous procurement descriptor `стандартный проход`; when it explicitly states a full passage, they SHALL expose `полнопроходной`. These descriptors SHALL be additive and SHALL not alter the product's source fields or matching decision semantics.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:27:- **WHEN** a ball-valve record has no recognised specialised execution and explicitly states full passage
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:32:- **WHEN** a ball-valve record explicitly identifies regulating execution and a non-full/reduced passage
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:33:- **THEN** its retrieval documents contain the regulating and `стандартный проход` descriptors and do not label that specialised execution as `стандартное исполнение`
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:37:The system SHALL use the same execution-enriched catalog representation for newly built dense index payload search text and for the in-memory BM25 lexical corpus. Query processing, hybrid fusion, reranker input, candidate filtering, and final result schemas SHALL remain unchanged.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:42:- **THEN** every newly indexed payload contains the execution-enriched dense search text and the BM25 corpus uses its corresponding enriched lexical text
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/specs/execution-aware-catalog-representation/spec.md:47:- **THEN** the system retains its existing retrieval text without ball-valve execution descriptors
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/design.md:3:See `proposal.md` for motivation. `documents.py` builds two related catalog representations: `build_search_text` is embedded and persisted in Qdrant payloads by `indexer.py`; `build_lexical_text` is tokenized by `BM25Store`. Both presently contain raw name, headline fields, and selected/all properties. The matcher already sends an unchanged source tender query through hybrid retrieval and the existing reranker. The query-constraint module separately infers ball-valve type from product evidence, but its execution vocabulary is not available to retrieval documents.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/design.md:10:- Make execution and passage wording available to both retrieval modalities without deleting or devaluing catalog evidence.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/design.md:19:- No inferred material, pressure, connection, temperature, product type, or special execution when source evidence is absent.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/design.md:29:### Treat ordinary execution as an exclusion-based, ball-valve-only descriptor
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/design.md:31:For catalog records identified as ball valves, append `стандартное исполнение` only when the recognised-specialisation allowlist finds no positive signal. Keep specialised and passage descriptors independent: a regulating, non-full product carries both its specific execution and `стандартный проход`, but never the ordinary-execution descriptor.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/design.md:47:- [Catalog wording is ambiguous or has an unrecognised special execution] → Emit no specialised descriptor unless an allowlisted explicit phrase is present; preserve raw fields for retrieval.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/design.md:48:- [An ordinary descriptor raises a specialised product unexpectedly] → Never apply ordinary execution when an allowlisted special marker is present; test mutual exclusion.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/tasks.md:3:- [x] 1.1 Implement a pure, bounded ball-valve execution-descriptor helper derived only from the product name and supported `Тип продукта`, `Тип прохода`, and `Управление` properties; verify unit tests cover ordinary, underground, regulating/Regula, cryogenic, gas-specific, electric-ready, full-passage, non-full/reduced-passage, and unrecognised inputs.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/tasks.md:4:- [x] 1.2 Enforce that specialised and ordinary execution descriptors are mutually exclusive, descriptors are stable in order, and non-ball-valve products receive none; verify focused unit tests assert each exclusion and raw-source preservation.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/tasks.md:9:- [x] 2.2 Append the same shared descriptors to `build_lexical_text` while retaining its compact existing fields; verify focused BM25/document tests show descriptor tokens are indexed and can rank a matching fixture above an otherwise comparable incompatible-execution fixture.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/proposal.md:3:The current retrieval documents preserve raw catalog text but lack a small, consistent representation of valve execution. As a result, ordinary tender requests can retrieve visually similar specialised variants, while catalog wording such as `Regula`, `для подземной установки`, or `под электропривод` is not expressed in the procurement vocabulary used by queries. This is now the highest-value untested retrieval mechanism: the hard-failure evidence includes specialised variants, whereas the previous selection filters and reranker-rubric experiments regressed safety or coverage.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/proposal.md:7:- Add deterministic, catalog-derived execution descriptors to dense and BM25 document representations for ball valves.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/proposal.md:9:- Represent ordinary versus explicitly specialised execution and explicit control-readiness concepts with stable, Russian procurement vocabulary.
openspec/changes/cycle-07-execution-aware-catalog-representation/proposal.md:16:- `execution-aware-catalog-representation`: Produces bounded, deterministic execution descriptors in catalog retrieval documents while preserving raw catalog evidence.

